{
  "summary": "The root cause of the persistent arrow key bug is NOT the CSS selector query (which was correctly fixed to use combined 'StageHeader, FeatureItem'). The actual bug is the items_pane.focus() call at the top of both action_focus_previous() (line 2768) and action_focus_next() (line 2794). This call immediately changes self.focused to the items_pane container, so when the code subsequently reads current = self.focused, it gets the container rather than the previously focused StageHeader/FeatureItem. Since the container is never in item_list, the 'current in item_list' check is always False, and navigation always falls through to focusing item_list[0] — the first item. Arrow keys appear broken because every press jumps to the first item instead of moving sequentially. The fix is to capture self.focused BEFORE calling items_pane.focus(), or better yet, remove the items_pane.focus() call entirely since individual items already receive focus directly. The dead except ValueError blocks and bare except Exception should also be cleaned up as previously identified."
}
